--TEST--
`Core\Path::fromCwd` throws a `RuntimeError` while a request is being answered, for a relative path and an absolute one alike, because a server's working directory is not the app's — `rule:programs/relative-paths-resolve-from-their-file`
--GET--
file=report.txt
--FILE--
<?nvs
array<string> $paths = ['report.txt', '/srv/report.txt'];
foreach ($paths as string $path) {
    try {
        echo Core\Path::fromCwd($path), "\n";
    } catch (RuntimeError $error) {
        echo $error->message, "\n";
    }
}
--EXPECT--
Core\Path::fromCwd cannot be used while answering a request, because a server's working directory is not the app's folder
help: write the path directly in the code, in quotes. It is then relative to the file that contains it. You can also build it with `Core\Path::join`
Core\Path::fromCwd cannot be used while answering a request, because a server's working directory is not the app's folder
help: write the path directly in the code, in quotes. It is then relative to the file that contains it. You can also build it with `Core\Path::join`
